Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:24:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: fusion splice diagram detail view (per-strand splice
 detail)

Adds a "View fusion diagram" action to each enclosure in the
Connectivity Diagram's node panel. Opens a full-width splice detail
styled after the standard OSP splice-closure convention (as seen in
tools like OZmap): each side cable drawn as a numbered, TIA-598
color-coded strand stub, with a colored curve per splice record
(fiber_splice_records: from_cable/from_strand -> to_cable/to_strand).
Multiple records sharing one input strand read naturally as a
splitter fan-out, no extra graphic required. Dashed/dimmed lines
mark splices not yet completed (splice_status != 'Spliced').

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
